  "summary": "Surrounding a spider with Hadamards changes its colour.",
  "description": "An X-spider is equal to a Z-spider with the same phase with a Hadamard gate on each of its legs (and vice versa). Combined with [Hadamard cancellation](../hadamard-cancellation/) this can also be seen as a rule for pushing a Hadamard gate through a spider, changing its colour.\n\nThis is the rule that turns any ZX-diagram into a graph-like diagram containing only Z-spiders and Hadamard edges.",
